WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.989
Stage twenty-one: start for free.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:10.982
The coach needs an AI. No technology to pick: just say what you already pay for.

3
00:00:11.082 --> 00:00:20.676
Claude, ChatGPT or GitHub Copilot: your plan is enough, at no extra cost. Nothing at all? OpenRouter, and its free trial.

4
00:00:21.526 --> 00:00:27.899
Three lines, just like stage one. Plus one option: the free trial, connected right away.

5
00:00:27.999 --> 00:00:33.198
The installer says it up front: zero euros, so no spending cap to set.

6
00:00:34.048 --> 00:00:42.341
An OpenRouter page opens. Sign in, or create an account, then authorize the coach. No key to create or copy.

7
00:00:42.441 --> 00:00:51.693
The key is stored on your machine, in a private file, and never shown. The coach checks the connection, and tells you what's left of today's quota.

8
00:00:52.543 --> 00:00:58.745
No terminal? In the macOS app, pick “Free trial”: the same connection, in one click.

9
00:01:00.543 --> 00:01:09.092
Zero euros, but a quota: fifty requests a day. And every tool call is one: a /log can use up to forty-eight.

10
00:01:09.192 --> 00:01:18.594
So plan on one /log and a few questions a day. The sync switches to watch mode: the AI only works when Garmin has something new.

11
00:01:19.444 --> 00:01:26.499
The catch: free model providers may keep your prompts, and the default model's provider says it trains on them.

12
00:01:26.599 --> 00:01:33.911
And the coach sends your HRV, your sleep, your injuries. No sensitive health data on the free trial.

13
00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:41.027
Convinced? Ten dollars of credit, just once: about a year of coaching, at eighty cents a month.

14
00:01:41.127 --> 00:01:47.094
And that first purchase lifts the free quota from fifty to a thousand requests a day.

15
00:01:49.644 --> 00:01:54.417
To go further: the “Choosing your AI” page of the documentation.
